# Git Commit Preparation

Before making any git commit in this project, always run:

```bash
python scripts/prepare_commit.py
```

## One-time developer setup

The script reads your package manager and environment name from a local config file
that is gitignored. Copy the example and fill in your own values:

```bash
cp dev_config.yaml.example dev_config.yaml
```

Then edit `dev_config.yaml`:

```yaml
package_manager: conda   # or: venv, virtualenv, poetry, pipenv
env_name: adt_py310      # your environment name
```

After that, `python scripts/prepare_commit.py` requires no arguments.

## CLI override (optional)

You can also pass values directly, which takes precedence over the config file:

```bash
python scripts/prepare_commit.py --package-manager conda --env-name adt_py310
python scripts/prepare_commit.py --package-manager venv  --env-name .venv
```

This script must complete successfully before staging and committing changes.

## User confirmation required

NEVER create a git commit unless the user has explicitly asked you to commit. If the user has not clearly requested a commit, always ask for confirmation before proceeding.
